{
  "tema": 7426,
  "slug": "comertelo",
  "titulo": "Reflexive and direct object pronouns with infinitives, gerunds and commands",
  "subtitulo": "Quiero comérmelo. Está bebiéndoselas. ¡Cómetelo!",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "With pronominal verbs (comerse, beberse, leerse, cortarse), the reflexive pronoun comes first, then the direct object: me lo, te las, se los. Attach both to infinitives, gerunds and affirmative commands (with an accent), or put them before the conjugated verb.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Some verbs take a reflexive pronoun to **intensify** (**comerse, beberse, leerse, tomarse**). Add a direct object pronoun and you get two: the **reflexive goes first**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "reflexive (me, te, se, nos)",
            "+",
            "direct object (lo, la, los, las)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "infinitive / gerund",
              "texto": "Attached (**comérmelo, bebiéndoselas**) or before the conjugated verb (**me lo quiero comer**, **se las está bebiendo**)."
            },
            {
              "forma": "affirmative command",
              "texto": "Always attached: **¡cómetelo!**, **¡bébetela!**"
            },
            {
              "forma": "conjugated verb / negative command",
              "texto": "Before: **me lo comí**, **no te lo comas**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Attaching two pronouns adds a syllable, so the stressed vowel takes an accent: **comérmelo, cortártelo, bebiéndoselas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: reflexive first, then the thing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Tengo un libro nuevo y quiero ==leérmelo== pronto.",
              "en": "I have a new book and I want to read it soon."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tu pelo está larguísimo. Deberías ==cortártelo==.",
              "en": "Your hair is super long. You should get it cut."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hay tres copas en la mesa y ella está ==bebiéndoselas== todas.",
              "en": "There are three glasses on the table and she's drinking them all."
            },
            {
              "es": "Déjame papitas. Te ==las== estás comiendo todas.",
              "en": "Leave me some chips. You're eating them all."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Cómetelo== todo!",
              "en": "Eat it all up!"
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==te lo== comas.",
              "en": "Don't eat it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
